   "text": "The drawing shows chlorhexidine digluconate: one chlorhexidine molecule and two gluconic acid molecules, drawn as separate components.\n\n**Chlorhexidine part (bottom):**\n- Two 4-chlorophenyl rings are each attached through an NH to a guanidine carbon.\n- Each of those guanidine carbons is joined to a second guanidine unit through an N=C link, giving a biguanide group on each side.\n- The two biguanides are connected by a chain of six CH2 groups.\n\n**Gluconic acid parts (top):** each is HOOC\u2013CH(OH)\u2013CH(OH)\u2013CH(OH)\u2013CH(OH)\u2013CH2OH. From the hashed and wedged OH bonds, I assigned CIP descriptors of 2R, 3S, 4R, 5R, which is D-gluconic acid. I then used the standard D-gluconic acid SMILES for the stereo.\n\nSMILES: NC(N)=NCCCCCCN=C(N)N=C(N)Nc1ccc(Cl)cc1.C([C@H]([C@H]([C@@H]([C@H](C(=O)O)O)O)O)O)O.C([C@H]([C@H]([C@@H]([C@H](C(=O)O)O)O)O)O)O\n\nI wrote the biguanide groups in a shorter, tautomerically different arrangement from the drawing, so the chlorhexidine part needs correcting to match it atom for atom. The drawn connectivity is Clc1ccc(NC(N)=NC(N)=NCCCCCCN=C(N)N=C(N)Nc2ccc(Cl)cc2)cc1.\n\nSMILES: Clc1ccc(NC(N)=NC(N)=NCCCCCCN=C(N)N=C(N)Nc2ccc(Cl)cc2)cc1.C([C@H]([C@H]([C@@H]([C@H](C(=O)O)O)O)O)O)O.C([C@H]([C@H]([C@@H]([C@H](C(=O)O)O)O)O)O)O"
